    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d456">

                <pb facs="0529" n="517" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg517"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Portugal/854: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Fish</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-09T23:00:00-04:00">April 9, 1943—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>618. Your 744, April 3, 11 a.m.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d456-f1"/> Immediately upon
                    conclusion of surcharge controversy, it is requested that you open negotiations
                    on wolfram agreement along lines detailed in the Department’s 228 of February
                    12, 7 p.m. If your British colleague lacks parallel instructions, or if in your
                    judgment intervening events require an altered approach, please telegraph
                    urgently.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
